1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,472
The Curiosity Club.

2
00:00:02,472 --> 00:00:04,714
Episode 40.

3
00:00:04,714 --> 00:00:07,649
The Museum of Better Questions.

4
00:00:07,649 --> 00:00:10,543
Here is something to listen for.

5
00:00:10,543 --> 00:00:14,932
Why did the club display some of its earlier mistaken ideas?

6
00:00:14,932 --> 00:00:16,453
Ready?

7
00:00:16,453 --> 00:00:18,559
Let us find out.

8
00:00:18,559 --> 00:00:23,084
The Curiosity Club opens a small exhibition for families.

9
00:00:23,084 --> 00:00:26,345
Maya stands beside the paper bridge.

10
00:00:26,345 --> 00:00:29,198
Leo manages the model boat.

11
00:00:29,198 --> 00:00:33,491
Pip welcomes visitors with a sign: Questions are free.

12
00:00:33,491 --> 00:00:35,747
Please take more than one.

13
00:00:35,747 --> 00:00:38,749
A younger child points at the bridge.

14
00:00:38,749 --> 00:00:40,747
Is this yours?

15
00:00:40,747 --> 00:00:43,410
It is ours, Maya says.

16
00:00:43,410 --> 00:00:46,548
We tested different folds together.

17
00:00:46,548 --> 00:00:50,230
Another visitor asks why the clay boat floats.

18
00:00:50,230 --> 00:00:54,347
Leo explains the shape and the water it pushes aside.

19
00:00:54,347 --> 00:00:59,429
When he forgets a word, he uses a simple sentence and points to the model.

20
00:00:59,429 --> 00:01:04,239
At the animal table, visitors guess which creature has three hearts.

21
00:01:04,239 --> 00:01:09,741
At the space table, a lamp and a ball show changing views of the Moon's bright side.

22
00:01:09,741 --> 00:01:12,961
Pip has made a wall of earlier guesses.

23
00:01:12,961 --> 00:01:15,271
The Sun goes to bed.

24
00:01:15,271 --> 00:01:18,627
Camels keep drinking water in their humps.

25
00:01:18,627 --> 00:01:21,358
Penguins are fish in jackets.

26
00:01:21,358 --> 00:01:23,722
Why display mistakes?

27
00:01:23,722 --> 00:01:25,883
a parent asks.

28
00:01:25,883 --> 00:01:31,127
Because we learned to change our ideas when we found better evidence, Maya says.

29
00:01:31,127 --> 00:01:34,157
The final table has blank cards.

30
00:01:34,157 --> 00:01:37,934
Visitors write something they would like to understand.

31
00:01:37,934 --> 00:01:44,184
Soon, the box is full of questions about music, oceans, buildings, and everyday life.

32
00:01:44,184 --> 00:01:48,084
Leo reads one: Why do we keep asking questions?

33
00:01:48,084 --> 00:01:50,366
Pip thinks carefully.

34
00:01:50,366 --> 00:01:53,573
Because each answer opens another door.

35
00:01:53,573 --> 00:01:57,622
Maya switches off the exhibition lamp at closing time.

36
00:01:57,622 --> 00:02:01,820
The real Sun has not gone to bed, she reminds Leo.

37
00:02:01,820 --> 00:02:04,116
I know, he says.

38
00:02:04,116 --> 00:02:06,671
But I am ready for dinner.

39
00:02:06,671 --> 00:02:11,141
Some questions, Pip announces, return every single day.

40
00:02:11,141 --> 00:02:14,157
Now, a little more to discover.

41
00:02:14,157 --> 00:02:18,817
Learning can connect observation, explanation, and checking.

42
00:02:18,817 --> 00:02:25,394
A model helps communicate an idea, while evidence helps decide whether the explanation fits.

43
00:02:25,394 --> 00:02:29,144
Revising a mistaken idea is part of learning.

44
00:02:29,144 --> 00:02:35,163
A useful question can be small and ordinary; it does not have to be about a distant planet.

45
00:02:35,163 --> 00:02:38,192
Let us hear the main idea again.

46
00:02:38,192 --> 00:02:43,206
The exhibition brought together bridges, boats, animals, and space.

47
00:02:43,206 --> 00:02:49,470
The club explained its discoveries, remembered earlier mistakes, and collected new questions.

48
00:02:49,470 --> 00:02:54,035
Curiosity continued after the last display was packed away.

49
00:02:54,035 --> 00:02:57,038
Here are three useful expressions.

50
00:02:57,038 --> 00:03:00,081
You can listen, or say them with me.

51
00:03:00,081 --> 00:03:01,956
It is ours.

52
00:03:01,956 --> 00:03:04,171
We made it together.

53
00:03:04,171 --> 00:03:06,046
It is ours.

54
00:03:06,046 --> 00:03:08,260
We made it together.

55
00:03:08,260 --> 00:03:11,711
I used to think that, but now I understand.

56
00:03:11,711 --> 00:03:15,163
I used to think that, but now I understand.

57
00:03:15,163 --> 00:03:18,097
What would you like to find out next?

58
00:03:18,097 --> 00:03:21,032
What would you like to find out next?

59
00:03:21,032 --> 00:03:23,899
Remember our listening question?

60
00:03:23,899 --> 00:03:28,288
Why did the club display some of its earlier mistaken ideas?

61
00:03:28,288 --> 00:03:30,475
Here is the answer.

62
00:03:30,475 --> 00:03:36,114
The mistakes showed how the children changed their thinking after gathering evidence and learning more.

63
00:03:36,114 --> 00:03:39,904
And here is a question just for your imagination.

64
00:03:39,904 --> 00:03:45,230
Which idea from the Curiosity Club would you most like to explain to someone else?

65
00:03:45,230 --> 00:03:48,396
There is more than one possible answer.

66
00:03:48,396 --> 00:03:51,548
Keep wondering, and see you next time.
